---
title: "Prepare a device and NAHPU"
sidebar:
  order: 1
---

Prepare the installation, power, and essential settings before fieldwork.

## Steps

{% steps %}

1. Install or update NAHPU while reliable internet is available.
2. Charge the device and power banks, then confirm enough free storage.
3. Open `Settings` and choose the catalog format, event methods, site vocabularies, and specimen options needed by the team.
4. Test the camera, GPS, file picker, and intended backup destination.
5. Run one mock catalog session and correct the setup before departure.
{% /steps %}

{% aside type="tip" %}

Keep the device offline when connectivity is not needed to conserve power and reduce exposure.

{% /aside %}

